From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:19:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: sg-pc phone logic from the original Game.exe (10:37,
 phone button, mails, address book)

STEINS;GATE (Steam) could not get past the prologue: instruction 10:37 (the phone) was a stub, and the scripts wait
on the native phone, e.g. the address book macro called in SG00_01 loops until GlobalVars[6822] names the contact at
row GlobalVars[6821]. The phone is now translated from the original routines (addresses of the Steam Game.exe):

- SGHD::Phone (src/games/sghd/phone.*): all 10:37 sub instructions (0x467f60): mail state bits (0x454880 /
  0x454860), the mail, attachment, ringtone and wallpaper tables read from six script labels (0x45bcf0), inbox /
  sent lists, address book order and the contacts that can be called or mailed (0x4544e0, order table 0x52e9d8),
  the selected mail (0x454420), mail and answer line counts (0x45b8e0 / 0x45b840), contacts (0x44d4e0 /
  0x44d4a0), the mail that is answered by a word (0x45a7f0 / 0x45a880), callable / mailable contacts
  (0x459ca0), the address book row (0x454400), dialling (0x45a000, keys 0x52ea08), today's date (0x4544a0 /
  0x45bb90), and one frame of the open phone (0x459ce0): all 40 modes of the original (home, menu, inbox / sent
  lists, reading, answering, the phone trigger words, address book, call / mail, settings, wallpapers, ringtones,
  attachments: pictures, picture stories, text pages, music).
- The open / close counter GlobalVars[6801] and the unread check run once per frame (0x459a30, 0x44d850) through the
  new GameSpecificType.SGHD (sg-pc gamespecific.lua).
- The phone's 500 byte bit field (mail states, registered contacts) is kept in every save like in the original
  (0x45d1c0): MO6TWPC save file version 2 stores game data per entry (version 1 files are still read; their
  entries have no phone data, so S;G saves from before this change start with an empty phone).
- Phone button: the original sets PADcustom[22] to L2 | R2 (Z / C on the keyboard, 0x44ce30); the sg-pc profile now
  does the same, the scripts open the phone with it.
- The message wait sets flag 1611 while it waits for the player (the only time the phone may be opened) and clears
  it when the message advances (as 0x45f5a0); while the player has the phone open (flag 2610) the message waits.
- New game clears the phone (0x45c240 from the work clear of the init instruction).

Not done here: the phone is not drawn yet (next patch), mouse / touch hit areas of the phone (the phone is driven
with the pad / keyboard buttons, on Android through the host's on-screen keys), the keyboard walk over the words of
the phone trigger (needs the phone text layout), Steam achievements.

Checked on MuMu (Android 15, not a real device, original English data): new game, skip through the prologue (the
address book macro passes, 646 mails, 5 contacts), in SG01_03 the phone opens with Z, menu -> address book ->
PhoneWave -> call, the call scene follows; save and load keep the phone data.

TYN only.

